      "@type": "Dataset",
      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Custom Crating Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Custom crating operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the full published scope of the crating service across its pages. Company scope (published): custom-built crates and high-value item protection for domestic and export moves — each crate measured, built and fitted to the piece it protects, not a stock box. Inside the crate, the item is blocked, braced and cushioned so it cannot shift in transit. Crating covers the pieces that need more than padding: antiques, artwork, machinery parts and high-value equipment. The crate is the second of the three protection layers the export pages publish — first the item is wrapped, then the crate is built around it, then the whole shipment moves in one unbroken chain — and where a crated shipment crosses a border, the crate is built to ISPM 15 (International Standards for Phytosanitary Measures No. 15). Heavy and high-mass pieces in the 1,500 to 3,500 lb band are planned under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol with L/360 floor-deflection analysis, inside the same written flat-rate job. The service is dispatched from two home bases — Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV. Every crating job is quoted at one flat rate, agreed in writing before move day.",
